From: tfrecomp <tfrecomp@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:30:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] native: enumerate monitors and display modes through
 CoreGraphics

The headless monitor functions returned no monitor at all, so
IDXGIAdapter::EnumOutputs found nothing, there was no mode list, and a
swap chain never learned the refresh rate it paces SyncInterval with.

An HMONITOR is now a CGDirectDisplayID.  The monitors are the online
displays that do not mirror another one (the list of active displays is
empty while the display sleeps); output 0 is the main display.  Desktop
coordinates and mode sizes are in points of the global display space.
The mode list is the current mode plus every mode CoreGraphics calls
usable for the desktop, without duplicates.  Modes are reported only,
never set.

util now links CoreGraphics and CoreFoundation in native builds.
